The caller aborts the signal 120 ms after calling `retry`, while it is in the 200 ms backoff wait. What happens?

```js
async function retry(fn, { retries = 3, signal } = {}) {
  for (let i = 0; ; i++) {
    try { return await fn(signal); }
    catch (err) {
      if (i >= retries || signal?.aborted) throw err;
      await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 2 ** i * 100));
    }
  }
}
```

